## Find the slope of PA
$A(-5,0)$, $P(-4,3)$, $B(5,0)$.
m_{PA} &= \frac{3 - 0}{-4 - (-5)}
&= \frac{3}{1}
&= 3
## Find the slope of PB
m_{PB} &= \frac{0 - 3}{5 - (-4)}
&= \frac{-3}{9}
&= -\frac{1}{3}
## Multiply the slopes
m_{PA} \times m_{PB} &= 3 \times \left(-\frac{1}{3}\right)
&= -1
The product of the slopes is $-1$, so $PA \perp PB$ and the triangle is right-angled at $P$.
ANSWER: \angle APB = 90^\circ

## Use the distance formula with A(2, 1) and D(1, 3)
|AD| &= \sqrt{(1-2)^2 + (3-1)^2}
&= \sqrt{(-1)^2 + 2^2}
&= \sqrt{1 + 4}
&= \sqrt{5}
ANSWER: |AD| = \sqrt{5}

## Find |CD| using C(5, 5) and D(1, 3)
|CD| &= \sqrt{(1-5)^2 + (3-5)^2}
&= \sqrt{16 + 4}
&= \sqrt{20}
## Area of a rectangle is length times width
\text{Area} &= |CD| \times |AD|
&= \sqrt{20} \times \sqrt{5}
&= \sqrt{100}
&= 10
ANSWER: 10 \text{ square units}

## Divide the area by the area one litre covers
\text{Litres} &= \frac{497.77}{12.25}
&= 40.63
## Round to the nearest litre
&\approx 41
ANSWER: 41\text{ litres}

## Slope of [AB]
Slope $= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$, with $A(1,-2)$ and $B(4,2)$.
m_{AB} &= \frac{2-(-2)}{4-1}
&= \frac{4}{3}
## Slope of [DE]
Use $D(6,-6)$ and $E(15,6)$.
m_{DE} &= \frac{6-(-6)}{15-6}
&= \frac{12}{9}
&= \frac{4}{3}
## Conclude
The slopes are equal, so the segments are parallel.
ANSWER: m_{AB} = m_{DE} = \frac{4}{3} \Rightarrow [AB] \parallel [DE]

## Use the distance formula
$A(1,-2)$ and $B(4,2)$.
|AB| &= \sqrt{(4-1)^2 + (2-(-2))^2}
&= \sqrt{3^2 + 4^2}
&= \sqrt{9 + 16}
&= \sqrt{25}
&= 5
ANSWER: |AB| = 5\text{ units}

## Divide the matching sides
Scale factor = image length $\div$ original length. $[DE]$ is the image of $[AB]$.
k &= \frac{|DE|}{|AB|}
&= \frac{15}{5}
&= 3
ANSWER: k = 3

## Mean of the Remain values
Mean $= \dfrac{\sum x}{n}$, with $n = 6$ age groups.
\text{Remain mean} &= \frac{73+62+52+44+43+40}{6}
&= \frac{314}{6}
&= 52.33
## Mean of the Leave values
\text{Leave mean} &= \frac{27+38+48+56+57+60}{6}
&= \frac{286}{6}
&= 47.67
ANSWER: \text{Remain} = 52.33\%,\ \text{Leave} = 47.67\%

## Test x = 1 in the terms from part (a)
The terms are $x^2$, $5x-8$, $x+8$. For $x = 1$ they are $1$, $-3$, $9$.
r &= \frac{-3}{1}
r &= -3
$|r| > 1$, so this series has no sum to infinity. Reject $x = 1$.
## Test x = 8 in the terms from part (a)
For $x = 8$ the terms are $8^2$, $5(8)-8$, $8+8$, that is $64$, $32$, $16$.
r &= \frac{32}{64}
r &= \frac{1}{2}
$|r| < 1$, so the sum to infinity exists. Here $x = 8$, $a = 64$ and $r = \tfrac{1}{2}$.
## Use the sum to infinity formula
S_\infty &= \frac{a}{1-r}
&= \frac{64}{1 - \frac{1}{2}}
&= \frac{64}{\frac{1}{2}}
&= 128
ANSWER: x = 8, \quad S_\infty = 128
